<%# BAST acceptance register (module 8 part 8.9; PRD §4.2/§4.3).

    WHAT THIS SCREEN HAS TO MAKE OBVIOUS, because the whole revenue feature depends on it:

    1. THE ACCEPTED PERCENTAGE IS THE REVENUE BASIS. Not the internal tick %. The header states the
       figure and explains the difference, so the reader sees the gap rather than being told about it.
    2. ONLY `accepted` COUNTS. The status column is the workflow, and a `submitted` certificate is
       visibly NOT yet revenue — the chip is amber, not green.
    3. A CERTIFICATE CANNOT BE CREATED AS ACCEPTED. That is decision A, so the record form has no
       status field at all and this page says so.
    4. AN ACCEPTED CERTIFICATE IS FROZEN. No edit or delete control is offered for one, because the
       basis revenue was computed from must not change underneath it.

    Receives: project, summary ({rows, counts, acceptedPct, rawAcceptedPct, overlapping}), caps,
    saved, savedStatus, error. %>
<% if (typeof error !== 'undefined' && error) { %>
<div class="errb"><div class="errb-tx"><p><b>Not done.</b> <%= error %></p></div></div>
<% } %>

<% if (!project) { %>
<div class="card"><div class="fbody">
  <p><b>No project is in scope for your account, so there is nothing to show.</b></p>
  <p class="dim" style="margin:6px 0 0">
    A progress certificate belongs to a project. Ask an Administrator to assign you to one.
  </p>
</div></div>
<% } else { %>

<% if (saved) { %>
<div class="note ok"><svg><use href="#i-check"/></svg><b>Recorded as a draft.</b>
  It does not count towards revenue until it is submitted and a Project Manager accepts it — that is
  the check that makes the client's sign-off real.</div>
<% } %>
<% if (savedStatus === 'submitted') { %>
<div class="note ok"><svg><use href="#i-check"/></svg><b>Submitted.</b>
  It is now waiting for a Project Manager to accept it against the signed paper.</div>
<% } %>
<% if (savedStatus === 'accepted') { %>
<div class="note ok"><svg><use href="#i-check"/></svg><b>Accepted.</b>
  This percentage is now part of the revenue basis the POC method reads.</div>
<% } %>
<% if (savedStatus === 'rejected') { %>
<div class="note ok"><svg><use href="#i-check"/></svg><b>Rejected.</b>
  It counts for nothing. Record a new certificate that supersedes it — a rejected certificate is kept
  as a record and cannot be revived.</div>
<% } %>

<div class="grid k4">
  <div class="card kpi"><div class="lbl"><svg><use href="#i-check"/></svg>Client accepted</div>
    <div class="v"><%= summary.acceptedPct %>%</div><div class="f">BAST certificates — the revenue basis</div></div>
  <div class="card kpi"><div class="lbl"><svg><use href="#i-file"/></svg>Awaiting acceptance</div>
    <div class="v"><%= summary.counts.submitted %></div><div class="f">submitted, not yet signed</div></div>
  <div class="card kpi"><div class="lbl"><svg><use href="#i-swap"/></svg>Drafts</div>
    <div class="v"><%= summary.counts.draft %></div><div class="f">not yet submitted</div></div>
  <div class="card kpi"><div class="lbl"><svg><use href="#i-lock"/></svg>Rejected</div>
    <div class="v"><%= summary.counts.rejected %></div><div class="f">count for nothing</div></div>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <div class="card-hd">
    <h2>What the client has accepted</h2>
    <span class="r"><%= summary.counts.accepted %> accepted certificate<%= summary.counts.accepted === 1 ? '' : 's' %></span>
  </div>
  <div class="fbody">
    <p><b>The accepted figure is what revenue is calculated from.</b> It is the percentage the client
    has put its name to on a certificate — not the progress your team has ticked off internally.</p>
    <p style="margin:8px 0 0" class="dim">
      The two are different things on purpose: the internal figure is an estimate of work done, this
      one is a signed acceptance. Revenue uses <b>this</b> one, so a month where the client has
      accepted nothing recognises nothing — however much work the team has finished.
    </p>
    <% if (summary.overlapping) { %>
    <p style="margin:10px 0 0"><b class="wn">
      The certificates total <%= summary.rawAcceptedPct %>% before capping. Revenue is capped at 100%
      so it can never exceed the contract — but overlapping certificates are worth a look.
    </b></p>
    <% } %>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <div class="card-hd">
    <h2>Certificates</h2>
    <span class="r">in the order they were issued</span>
  </div>
  <div class="tw">
    <table>
      <thead><tr>
        <th>#</th><th>Certificate</th><th>WBS line</th><th>Description</th>
        <th class="r">Accepted %</th><th>Signed</th><th>Handover</th><th>Accepted</th>
        <th>Status</th><th></th>
      </tr></thead>
      <tbody>
      <% if (!summary.rows.length) { %>
        <tr><td colspan="10" class="dim">
          No certificates recorded yet. Until one is accepted, revenue recognition has nothing to
          work from and will read 0%.
        </td></tr>
      <% } %>
      <% summary.rows.forEach(function(c) { %>
        <% const chip = c.status === 'accepted' ? 'ok'
             : (c.status === 'submitted' ? 'wn' : (c.status === 'rejected' ? 'bd' : 'nt')); %>
        <tr>
          <td class="dim"><%= c.sequence == null ? '' : c.sequence %></td>
          <td><b><%= c.certificate_no || '—' %></b></td>
          <td><%= c.wbs_code ? (c.wbs_code + ' ' + (c.wbs_name || '')) : '' %><% if (!c.wbs_code) { %><span class="dim">whole project</span><% } %></td>
          <td><%= c.description || '' %><% if (!c.description) { %><span class="dim">—</span><% } %></td>
          <td class="r"><b><%= c.percentage_progress == null ? '—' : c.percentage_progress + '%' %></b></td>
          <td><%= c.document_date || '' %><% if (!c.document_date) { %><span class="dim">—</span><% } %></td>
          <td><%= c.handover_date || '' %><% if (!c.handover_date) { %><span class="dim">—</span><% } %></td>
          <td><%= c.accepted_date || '' %><% if (!c.accepted_date) { %><span class="dim">—</span><% } %></td>
          <td><span class="chip <%= chip %>"><%= c.status.toUpperCase() %></span></td>
          <td>
            <% if (c.status === 'draft' && caps.canManageAcceptance) { %>
              <form method="post" action="/acceptance/<%= c.id %>/submit" style="display:inline">
                <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
                <button class="btn" type="submit">Submit</button>
              </form>
            <% } else if (c.status === 'submitted' && caps.canApproveAcceptance) { %>
              <form method="post" action="/acceptance/<%= c.id %>/accept" style="display:inline">
                <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
                <button class="btn pri" type="submit">Accept</button>
              </form>
              <form method="post" action="/acceptance/<%= c.id %>/reject" style="display:inline">
                <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
                <button class="btn" type="submit">Reject</button>
              </form>
            <% } else if (c.status === 'submitted') { %>
              <span class="dim">a Project Manager accepts this</span>
            <% } else if (c.status === 'accepted') { %>
              <span class="dim">counted</span>
            <% } else { %>
              <span class="dim">—</span>
            <% } %>
          </td>
        </tr>
      <% }); %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <div class="card-hd"><h2>How a certificate becomes revenue</h2><span class="r">PRD §4.3</span></div>
  <div class="fbody">
    <p><b>Record → Submit → Accept.</b> A certificate is always recorded as a <b>draft</b>; nobody can
    create one already accepted. That is deliberate — the difference between &ldquo;we submitted
    it&rdquo; and &ldquo;the client accepted it&rdquo; is the whole point of the figure.</p>
    <p style="margin:8px 0 0">
      <b>Submitting</b> says the paper has gone to the client. <b>Accepting</b> records that they
      signed it, and that is a Project Manager's decision, not the recorder's.
    </p>
    <p style="margin:8px 0 0" class="dim">
      An accepted certificate cannot be edited or deleted — it is the basis the revenue was
      calculated from. If it was wrong, record a new certificate: the sequence keeps the order clear,
      and the revenue figure will follow the corrected total.
    </p>
    <p style="margin:8px 0 0" class="dim">
      A <b>rejected</b> certificate counts for nothing and cannot be accepted later. It is kept so the
      register shows what happened.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<% } %>

<svg style="display:none" aria-hidden="true"><defs>
<symbol id="i-info" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M12 3a9 9 0 1 0 0 18 9 9 0 0 0 0-18Zm-2.6 2.4h1.2v12.1H9.5z"/></symbol>
</defs></svg>
